    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d108">

                <pb facs="0174" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg98"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.001Y9/15</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Minister to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chinese Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 6, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: It becomes my painful duty to inform you
                    that His Excellency Yuan Shih-Kai, President of the Republic of China, died at
                    Peking on the morning of the 6th instant at 10 o’clock, Vice President Li
                    Yuan-hung, in accordance with the provisions of the Constitution of the
                    Republic, assuming the duties of the high office and acting as President—who
                    will formally take the oath of office as President on the morning of the 7th
                    instant at 10 o’clock.</p>
                <p>In communicating to you this sorrowful intelligence,</p>
                <p>I avail [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vi Kyuin Wellington Koo</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
